From f2eed0a655d52908275307389230c61987c1a557 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 20:53:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v2.2.2: per-device connection-health metrics + analytics
 export (Splunk/Prometheus/Datadog/etc.)

Adds a robust per-device connection-health signal and the ability to stream it
to an analytics engine, plus a retain/send-mode control on Long-Term Storage.
Implements the backlogged "Traffic Analyzer -> Splunk connection-health export".

Collector (rtrafd):
- NCLI 64 -> 192 (100-150 client LANs); DB_VER 1 -> 2 (dbhdr_t layout changed;
  a v1 rtraf.db is safely parked as .prev).
- New opt-in health probe (nvram rtraf_hprobe): per-device latency/jitter/loss
  via a BATCHED in-process ICMP echo (one non-blocking raw socket, replies
  drained across ticks over a 2s window - never fork-per-ping) + per-device TCP
  connection count/established-state from conntrack (state survives HW offload;
  retransmits deliberately NOT collected - cannot be sourced cleanly). Publishes
  /tmp/rtraf/health.json + /tmp/rtraf/metrics.prom (OpenMetrics) each cycle, and
  appends a rotated healthhist.log to the durable store (unless export-only).
  GOTCHA: <netinet/ip_icmp.h> #defines BSD macros icmp_id/icmp_cksum that collide
  with C identifiers - health-probe ids renamed hp_*.

Exporter (rc/rexport.c, NEW; wired via rc.h/Makefile/services.c/init.c):
- cru-scheduled pusher (mirrors rwatch/rwarden). Shapes health.json per engine
  preset - Splunk HEC / Datadog / Dynatrace / Elastic / Generic / OTLP push, or
  RFC5424-over-TLS syslog - and POSTs with curl. TLS verify ON unless
  reaper_export_tlsverify=0; token kept out of ps/logs via a 0600 curl -K config;
  optional MAC hashing. Prometheus is pull, so the pusher no-ops for it.

httpd (web.c):
- do_reaper_export_cgi (status/save/test; token returned masked) + reaper_export
  store integration (store_set/store_status gain the retain/send mode).
- do_reaper_metrics_cgi: public (NULL auth) OpenMetrics endpoint, ?token= gated
  on reaper_export_scrape_token, for Prometheus scrape.
- reaper_traffic.cgi f= allowlist gains "health" (payload preview).

UI: new Reaper_Analytics.asp (Administration -> Data Export, self-themed native
page; registered in reaper_inject.c reaper_native[] + menuTrees/menuTree.js) with
engine presets, endpoint/token, TLS toggle, metric selection, interval, preview,
and Test Connection. Reaper_Storage.asp gains the Off/Store+Export/Export-only
mode card. 25 dicts gain RANL_00-45 + RDST_50-59 in lockstep (6249 each).

New nvram (all "unset = safe default", no defaults.c): rtraf_hprobe, rtraf_hint,
reaper_export_mode (off|both|exportonly), reaper_export_{engine,url,token,
tlsverify,interval,metrics,index,source,scrape_token,maskmac}. Export OFF by
default.

Validated: BE96U MCP build MAKE_EXIT=0, no errors in any changed file; host-gcc
ICMP check; generated rexport.sh sh -n clean; both pages ASCII-0 + JS-parse
clean; dicts lockstep. Metal + noMCP build + 5-model fan-out owed.
